__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Example/template env files carry no secrets and MUST be tracked —
# without this negation portal/.env.local.example was silently ignored.
!*.env*.example
!.env.*.example
!scripts/uat/.env.uat.template
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
.next/
dist/
build/
coverage/
.pytest_cache/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.log
logs/

# Scratch/debug scratchpads — never commit (once held a real admin JWT; see
# docs/SECURITY_17A_TOKEN_PURGE.md). Ignored everywhere in the tree.
.tmp_bugs/
**/.tmp_bugs/
tmp/
storage/
# Track the Go ``internal/storage/`` package — the generic
# ``storage/`` rule above was meant for data dirs (./data/storage,
# etc.), not Go source. Exception must come AFTER the broader rule.
!services/chat-edge-api/internal/storage/
!services/chat-edge-api/internal/storage/**
# Same fix for the desktop's C# Storage source — the ``storage/`` rule
# matched it case-insensitively on Windows, leaving these core files
# UNTRACKED (a fresh clone wouldn't build). Re-include the source dir.
!SranDesktop/src/SranDesktop.Infrastructure/Storage/
!SranDesktop/src/SranDesktop.Infrastructure/Storage/**
# ...and the matching TEST directory, for the same reason. This one bit later:
# four test sources sat there untracked and did not even appear in git status,
# so `git add -A` skipped them without a word. A rule meant for data directories
# must never be left to match source by accident.
!SranDesktop/src/SranDesktop.Tests/Storage/
!SranDesktop/src/SranDesktop.Tests/Storage/**
# ...and the fourth occurrence: the platform split moved the C# Storage source
# into a NEW SranDesktop.Infrastructure.Windows project, and the same broad
# `storage/` rule swallowed it too — DpapiCredentialStore.cs sat untracked, so
# a fresh clone of the kept sidecar path would not build. Re-include it, same
# as the three above. (The broad rule itself should be narrowed to data dirs;
# that is a separate, reviewable change — not made mid-commit-of-untracked-work.)
!SranDesktop/src/SranDesktop.Infrastructure.Windows/Storage/
!SranDesktop/src/SranDesktop.Infrastructure.Windows/Storage/**
uploads/
*.sqlite3
admin-ui/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
backend/uploads/

# Perf-baseline track (deferred) — source lives on branch
# archive/uncommitted-20260423 in perf/. Generated results and scratch
# directories are never tracked on main.
perf/
perf_audit_tmp/

# Local dev artifacts (DOM measurements, hero-tuning screenshots,
# debug request/response traces) — not project sources.
measure.js
hero-*.png
traces/

# Report & audit docs (root level)
*_REPORT.md
*_AUDIT_REPORT.md
*_VERIFICATION_REPORT.md
*_PLAN.md
*_LOG.md
BASELINE_STATUS.md
IMPLEMENTATION_ROADMAP.md
RUNBOOK.md
TASK_BOARD.md
POST_*.md
THREE_FIXES_REPORT.md
UX_CLEANUP_REPORT.md
RUNTIME_CONSOLIDATION_REPORT.md

# Shell test scripts
real-loop-test.sh
sran-pii-test.sh

# Rust sidecar build artifacts
dlp-sidecar/target/

# UAT seed output — contains raw API keys printed once by 02_seed_uat.py.
# Keep on disk only until copied into the customer's secret manager.
uat-seed-output.txt

# Secrets & local state (cross-cutting; defense in depth)
*.pem
*.key
credentials.dat
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
Thumbs.db
.vs/

# SranDesktop's Inno Setup script lives in build/ — a required build
# input, not an output. Re-include it past the generic ``build/`` rule
# above (dir first, then contents — same pattern as internal/storage).
!SranDesktop/build/
!SranDesktop/build/**

# FIX19 — same case again: the Electron app's electron-builder NSIS include
# (apps/desktop/build/installer.nsh) is a required build INPUT the config
# references, swallowed by the generic ``build/`` rule. Re-include it. (The
# electron-builder OUTPUT, apps/desktop/release/, stays ignored above.)
!apps/desktop/build/
!apps/desktop/build/**
# FIX20 — but the runtime config scripts/dist.js STAGES there for
# electron-builder (a copy of whatever config the build was pointed at — for
# a server build, a file that lives outside the repo) is a build artefact.
apps/desktop/build/desktop.config.json

# Local data and dev-server artifacts (dev-server*.log already matches *.log)
# ROOT-ANCHORED on purpose. Unanchored, ``data/`` matched at any depth and
# silently ignored backend/app/services/dlp/data/ -- the five corpora the
# detector engine loads at runtime (content_policy.py, thai_name_no_prefix.py,
# public_entity_registry.py). They sat tracked-but-ignored for months. The
# rule was only ever meant for the local ./data dir at the repo root.
# Same failure mode as ``storage/``; see the hand-written escapes at :32-47.
/data/
test-results/
.next-dev/
.next-fresh/

# Local pre-fix backup snapshots (multi-GB) - never commit
_retired-*/

# AI-workflow scratch files - keep out of the repo (2026-08-12 hygiene pass)
# Both spellings. PROMPT*.md matches a PREFIX only, so it never caught any
# of the 75 *_PROMPT.md task briefs it was added for -- they stayed tracked
# until the 2026-08-22 pass. The suffix form must be listed separately.
# The lowercase working briefs (prompt-fix33-*.md ...) only match PROMPT*.md
# because this checkout has core.ignorecase=true (Windows); a case-sensitive
# clone (Linux CI) would see them as untracked noise, so the lowercase rule
# is spelled out too (2026-09-03 pass).
PROMPT*.md
prompt-*.md
*_PROMPT.md
*_sandbox_*
scratchpad/
*.patch

# Build artifacts: installers and release binaries (2026-08-20 hygiene pass)
# Nothing here is source — every one is regenerable by the desktop build.
# The tree already carries a ~98 MB installer under releases/, which no rule
# covered: a single `git add -A` would put it in history permanently, and
# undoing that means rewriting history across every branch.
# SranDesktop/publish/ and SranDesktop/installer/ were already covered by
# SranDesktop/.gitignore:6-7; these extension rules are the repo-wide
# backstop for artifacts produced anywhere else, including releases/.
# Scoped by extension rather than by directory ON PURPOSE: releases/ is the
# desktop update channel and releases/latest.json is the live manifest whose
# history is the rollback path, so it must STAY TRACKED. A `releases/` rule
# would have swallowed it.
*.exe
*.msi
*.msix
*.appx
*.appxbundle
*.nupkg

# FIX19 — electron-builder output for the Electron desktop app. The installer
# .exe is already covered above, but the win-unpacked/ tree (app.asar, *.dll,
# *.pak, builder config) is not — this ignores the whole output dir. Note this
# is apps/desktop/release/ (singular, a build artefact), NOT the tracked
# releases/ desktop update channel.
/apps/desktop/release/

# Working documents: records of how the work got done, not how the system
# works (2026-08-22 hygiene pass). ROOT-ANCHORED so they cannot reach a
# same-named directory deeper in the tree, the way the old data/ rule did.
/audit/
/audit-functional/
/reports/
/sprint-reports/

# Staged release manifests. releases/latest.json is the LIVE manifest and
# stays tracked; the per-version staged files are build scratch that a
# ``git add -A`` would otherwise sweep in.
releases/*.staged.json

# Stray desktop icon. The build uses Assets/app.ico (csproj:12, iss:31);
# this one is referenced by nothing and has been committed by accident twice.
SranDesktop/src/SranDesktop.App/Assets/sran-app.ico

# Browser-bridge pairing token dropped into the unpacked extension folder by
# the desktop app (contains a secret) — never commit it.
pairing.json
**/browser-extension/pairing.json

# Owner hand-test session notes (working docs; kept on disk, never committed).
docs/OWNER_*.md
# Landing-redesign scratch/mock dir (design reference; the portal holds the shipped code).
_landing-redesign/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What belongs in the repo and what does not
#
#   IN:   source, tests, reusable tooling (scripts/probes/, backend/evals/),
#         architecture and contract docs (docs/*.md, docs/known-issues/)
#   OUT:  per-round working documents — reports (*_REPORT.md), task briefs
#         (PROMPT*.md), plans (PLAN_*.md); evidence gathered while verifying
#         a change (docs/fix*/, docs/audit/, docs/shots/); raw probe output
#         (scripts/probes/**/results/, *.json beside the probes, scripts/*.txt);
#         files a build step writes (apps/desktop/build/installer-defines.nsh)
#
# Everything under OUT stays on the author's disk; it is context for how a
# change was made, not a description of how the system works.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PLAN_*.md
docs/fix*/
docs/audit/
docs/shots/
scripts/probes/**/results/
scripts/probes/**/*.json
scripts/probes/router-compare/results*.md
scripts/*.txt
scripts/*.jsonl
apps/desktop/build/installer-defines.nsh
